    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "tbl_0017",
      "reading_order": 898,
      "section": "Pressure Switch Continuity Check",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 337.51629638671875,
        "t": 405.1341247558594,
        "r": 576.0411376953125,
        "b": 331.19775390625
      },
      "markdown": "| Pressure Switch Continuity Check   | Pressure Switch Continuity Check              |\n|------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| No Pressure                        | Switch Open - Infinite or High Resistance     |\n| Apply Pressure (Blow into hose*)   | Switch Closed - Continuity (less than 3 ohms) |"
    },
    {
      "type": "footnote",
      "id": "txt_0804",
      "reading_order": 899,
      "section": "Pressure Switch Continuity Check",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 339.0,
        "t": 328.82,
        "r": 577.51,
        "b": 301.2121008403361
      },
      "content": "* When you blow into the pressure hose that is connected to the switch, an audible 'click' can be heard indicating the switch has closed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0805",
      "reading_order": 900,
      "section": "Pressure Switch Continuity Check",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 539.6313,
        "t": 44.86829999999998,
        "r": 555.8369,
        "b": 32.765719354838666
      },
      "content": "n"
    }
  ]
}